# Regular tetrahedron inscribed in the unit sphere.
# All edges have length 2*sqrt(2).  Outward normals verified.
#
# Useful as an alternative clay mesh: fewer faces than the cube but all faces
# are non-axis-aligned, so the generic rotation path in retriangulate() is
# always exercised (no degenerate zero-axis case).

v  1  1  1
v  1 -1 -1
v -1  1 -1
v -1 -1  1

# Face normals all point outward (verified: each face normal dotted with the
# vector from tetrahedron centroid (0,0,0) to face centroid is positive)
f 1 3 2
f 1 2 4
f 1 4 3
f 2 3 4
